course: dictionary
lesson: 696
title: Banker: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Look at the clues: who is doing what, and where it happens. «In Monopoly the dice decide where you land; the banker handles the money but cannot choose squares.» Here the clues are Monopoly, dice and money, so a banker is the player who looks after the money in the game.
explain: In a bank, a banker is a person who works at a high level, deciding who can borrow money and how much interest to pay. Grown-ups might say «a bank manager» for the person you meet at a branch. The word banker can also mean something certain to win. If someone says «That team is a banker for the title», the clue is title: they mean the team is sure to win.
explain: Check your meaning. Put it in the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense. In the game sentence, "the player in charge of the money" fits. In the team sentence, "something sure to win" fits. If it does not fit, try another meaning.
fact: A banker can be a person who works in a bank and decides about loans and money.
fact: In games like Monopoly, the banker is the player in charge of the bank: they hand out money and take it in.
fact: «Banker» in UK informal talk means something certain to happen or win.
fact: «Being the banker in a game is a test of honesty, even though it is only a game.» Honesty means telling the truth and playing fair.
fact: Context clues, such as the words around a word, help you choose the right meaning.
exercise: «In Monopoly the dice decide where you land; the banker handles the money but cannot choose squares.» What job does the banker do in this game? | Decides which squares are on the board | *Hands out and takes in the money | Rolls the dice to decide where you land | Lends money to the people at the bank
exercise: In a bank, what does a banker decide? | Who wins a game of football | Which squares the other players land on | How tall the bank building should be | *Who can borrow money and how much interest to pay
exercise: Dad says, «That team is a banker for the title.» What does banker mean here? | The player in charge of the money in a game | A person who works in a bank | *Something certain to happen or win | A river bank where ducks swim
test: «Being the banker in a game is a test of honesty, even though it is only a game.» What does this sentence suggest? | *Handling the money fairly matters, even in a game | Games are never fair, so nobody cares | The banker always wins the game | Only grown-ups can be bankers
test: Ella's mum has a meeting with a banker about a loan. What is the banker most likely to decide? | *Whether she can borrow money and how much | Which squares she lands on in Monopoly | Who will win the football match | What colour the bank's doors are
exam: Sam is the banker, so he counts all the money. Which meaning of banker is this? | A person who works in a bank and lends money | Something certain to win | *The player in charge of the bank in a game | A bank of soil by a river
